# Phase 0 — Decisions Log (resolved 2026-05-06)

## 1. Single-instance lock under `SLAYZONE_STORE_DIR`

**Revised decision:** call `app.setPath('userData', getDataRoot())` early in main (before `app.whenReady`). Electron's lock + cookies + GPU cache + crash dumps all relocate to the right dir per instance. No skip needed.

Original (a) "skip lock when env set" rejected — `setPath` is the sustainable answer per CLAUDE.md. Phase 3 single-writer lockfile (per data-dir, race-safe) layers on top later.

## 2. `SLAYZONE_PORT` — defer

MCP and `@slayzone/server` will be one server (single WS multiplexing tRPC + MCP, master §4 Phase 3). Phase 0 ships only `getMcpPort()` + `getServerHost()`.

## 3. `SLAYZONE_HOST` — default `127.0.0.1`, warn on non-loopback

`console.warn` interim. Full trusted-net banner in Phase 3 per master §11b.

## 4. CLI env vars — **rename + consolidate**

**Decision:** rename `SLAYZONE_DB_DIR` → `SLAYZONE_STORE_DIR` (current name lies — dir holds DB + artifacts + project-icons + backups + Extensions + browser-extensions.json). Drop `SLAYZONE_DB_PATH` entirely. CLI derives file path: `<STORE_DIR>/slayzone[.dev].sqlite` based on `SLAYZONE_DEV`.

**Audit confirms safe.** All 10 `SLAYZONE_DB_PATH` consumers (7 files) compute `dbPath = path.join(dir, 'slayzone.dev.sqlite')` — fully derivable. Tests can swap `SLAYZONE_DB_PATH=dbPath` → `SLAYZONE_STORE_DIR=dir` + ensure `SLAYZONE_DEV=1`.

Hard rename. No backwards compat. Dev-only env var, no prod users.

## 5. `db/index.ts:65` legacy migration — skip + comment

Pre-rebrand migration reads Electron-default `userData`, not env override. Keep `app.getPath()`. Add comment.

After `setPath` decision (Q1): migration still works because `appData` is unaffected by `setPath('userData', ...)`. The new `userData` is now `getDataRoot()` — migration target. That's correct: legacy data should land in the new (overridable) data dir.
